Smaller leaks on every level load: the level's mesh vertex buffers, and three more

A level free drops its objects with the object arena and deletes its meshes, but some of what a load creates is never
released. Each full load (restarts, the studio and every level entry included) leaves behind:

- The vertex buffers of every mesh in the level. Load_WarMeshes builds each of the level's meshes with
  Mesh::BuildFromBsFile, which creates two Direct3D vertex buffers per mesh (the positions and the transformed
  vertices, 12 + 16 bytes per vertex). Load_FreeWarMeshes deletes the meshes, but Mesh::~Mesh frees only the face array
  and nothing releases the buffers, so the whole level's geometry buffers stay allocated (elastic objects' meshes,
  which go in the same table, included). This is likely the largest
  per-load leak after the iris texture (fixes/iris-mask-leak.patch).
- Road Runner (bipbip): PostLoadInit creates the two shared vertex buffers on every call, overwriting the previous
  ones, where every other shared buffer is created once.
- The rolling carpet: its belt set-up makes a new backup Texture on every load without deleting the previous one.
- Time_Init, called by Load_DAVnWAR on every load, makes a new Timer (0x28 bytes) without deleting the previous one.

This fix releases a mesh's buffers in its destructor (and nulls them in its constructor), creates the Road Runner's
buffers once, and deletes the previous rolling-carpet backup and Timer before making new ones. Behaviour is unchanged. The meshes elastic objects build are in the same mesh table (elastic.cpp puts them there),
so their buffers are released by the same destructor.

Touches: src/engine/mesh.cpp (Mesh::Mesh, Mesh::~Mesh), src/objects/bipbip.cpp (bipbip::PostLoadInit),
src/objects/rollingcarpet.cpp (RollingCarpet::InitBeltScroll), src/engine/time.cpp (Time_Init).

diff --git a/src/engine/mesh.cpp b/src/engine/mesh.cpp
index 4a1892c..5b08d0c 100644
--- a/src/engine/mesh.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/mesh.cpp
@@ -186,6 +186,8 @@ Mesh::Mesh()
 {
     app = 0;
     faces = 0;
+    vbPositions = 0;   /* FIX level-load-leaks: so that the destructor can release them */
+    vbTransformed = 0; /* FIX level-load-leaks */
 }
 
 /* 0x40c1db */
@@ -193,6 +195,12 @@ Mesh::~Mesh()
 {
     if (faces && faceCount > 0)
         delete[] faces;
+    /* FIX level-load-leaks: the original never released a mesh's two vertex buffers, so every level free left those
+     * of all the level's meshes behind. */
+    if (vbPositions)
+        vbPositions->Release();
+    if (vbTransformed)
+        vbTransformed->Release();
 }
 
 /* Two unused inline functions with an array new. They emit nothing, but VC6 numbers each array new's count
diff --git a/src/engine/time.cpp b/src/engine/time.cpp
index ba034a0..843a6e1 100644
--- a/src/engine/time.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/time.cpp
@@ -42,6 +42,8 @@ extern u32 g_gameFlags; /* 0x6ddf74  bit 0x40 = paused
  * Time_Update delta is 0) and zeroes the clock; the previous Timer is not deleted. */
 void Time_Init()
 {
+    if (g_pTimer) /* FIX level-load-leaks: Time_Init runs on every level load; the previous Timer was never deleted */
+        delete g_pTimer;
     g_pTimer = new Timer;
     g_pTimer->Stop();
     g_timeScale = 0x1000;
diff --git a/src/objects/bipbip.cpp b/src/objects/bipbip.cpp
index 87ff20a..7e545d0 100644
--- a/src/objects/bipbip.cpp
+++ b/src/objects/bipbip.cpp
@@ -150,13 +150,15 @@ void bipbip::PostLoadInit()
     desc.dwCaps = D3DVBCAPS_DONOTCLIP;
     desc.dwFVF = D3DFVF_XYZ;
     desc.dwNumVertices = 2;
-    g_pD3DAppMain->CreateVB(&desc, &g_bipbipVb);
+    if (!g_bipbipVb) /* FIX level-load-leaks: created once, as the other shared vertex buffers are */
+        g_pD3DAppMain->CreateVB(&desc, &g_bipbipVb);
     memset(&desc, 0, sizeof(desc));
     desc.dwSize = sizeof(desc);
     desc.dwCaps = D3DVBCAPS_DONOTCLIP;
     desc.dwFVF = D3DFVF_XYZRHW;
     desc.dwNumVertices = 2;
-    g_pD3DAppMain->CreateVB(&desc, &g_bipbipVbXf);
+    if (!g_bipbipVbXf) /* FIX level-load-leaks */
+        g_pD3DAppMain->CreateVB(&desc, &g_bipbipVbXf);
 }
 
